[[:db/add "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4" :answer/id #uuid "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4"] [:db/add "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4" :answer/value "\\frac{16}{15}"] [:db/ensure "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7"] [:db/add "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/choices "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4"] [:db/add "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/correct "bc894574-064a-5a40-a551-026f5aac56a4"] [:db/ensure "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/id #uuid "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa"] [:db/add "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{(x-3)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(4,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/add "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-\\frac{(x-3)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{-x^{2}+6x-9}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=-x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+6x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-9x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+3x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{9}{2}x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(4,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(4)&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}+3\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{9}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=-3+\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{9}{16}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{15}{16}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{15}{16}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{16}{15}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/answer-fields "2267e857-aa87-5e82-ac21-3bfa172671c7"] [:db/ensure "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/questions "0149a85e-1873-5267-84af-8709f99c27aa"] [:db/add "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355" :answer/id #uuid "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355"] [:db/add "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355" :answer/value "\\frac{27}{130}"] [:db/ensure "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355" :answer/validate] [:db/add "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8"] [:db/add "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/choices "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355"] [:db/add "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/correct "01827d3b-3746-5887-8b76-d50e0b44f355"] [:db/ensure "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/id #uuid "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275"] [:db/add "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{(x+1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(9,-\\frac{100}{3}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/add "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-\\frac{(x+1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{-x^{2}-2x-1}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=-x^{\\frac{3}{2}}-2x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(9,-\\frac{100}{3}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(9)&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}-\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{54}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{130}{27}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{130}{27}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{27}{130}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/answer-fields "692a0d7e-4c67-54cf-aa69-84cd36afb8e8"] [:db/ensure "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/questions "e664df6f-8587-5fd1-a057-f264471f4275"] [:db/add "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe" :answer/id #uuid "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe"] [:db/add "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe" :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}"] [:db/ensure "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe" :answer/validate] [:db/add "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c"] [:db/add "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/choices "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe"] [:db/add "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/correct "1471244c-d8d6-591a-a70d-46c73ac414fe"] [:db/ensure "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/id #uuid "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9"] [:db/add "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(1,9\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/add "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{x^{2}+4x+4}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+4x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+4x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(1,9\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(1)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(1\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\left(1\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2\\left(1\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}+2-2\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/answer-fields "6d31e2a3-d838-5cbf-a0e3-5001a3f62c6c"] [:db/ensure "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/questions "7e7d3211-8724-59e8-8faa-fdbf1204fed9"] [:db/add "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca" :answer/id #uuid "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca"] [:db/add "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca" :answer/value "\\frac{54}{275}"] [:db/ensure "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca" :answer/validate] [:db/add "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41"] [:db/add "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/choices "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca"] [:db/add "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/correct "80e360c7-5001-519a-9b67-d0ae691e9aca"] [:db/ensure "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/id #uuid "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40"] [:db/add "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(9,-\\frac{121}{3}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/add "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{-x^{2}-4x-4}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=-x^{\\frac{3}{2}}-4x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-4x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+2x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(9,-\\frac{121}{3}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(9)&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}-2\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{27}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{275}{54}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{275}{54}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{54}{275}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/answer-fields "cc5fc6c0-efa1-565f-ac70-326e6bcdfb41"] [:db/ensure "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/questions "70d823e6-b63f-5d22-93b3-c5be9a014e40"] [:db/add "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8" :answer/id #uuid "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8"] [:db/add "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}"] [:db/ensure "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c"] [:db/add "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/choices "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8"] [:db/add "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/correct "62449afb-c8bd-583f-a3bc-63ef0ad0b9a8"] [:db/ensure "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/id #uuid "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848"] [:db/add "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{(x-2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(4,-2\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/add "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-\\frac{(x-2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{-x^{2}+4x-4}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=-x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+4x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-4x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+2x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(4,-2\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(4)&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=-3+1+\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{7}{4}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/answer-fields "f4bbf3f8-da4e-5aa8-a373-a409bf7ceb1c"] [:db/ensure "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/questions "c3f077c2-6979-55f7-a9ea-baa931e5b848"] [:db/ensure 17592186092384 :knowledge-point/validate]]
